>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Dark Matter Galaxy Evolution Simulations<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>N-body, hydrodynamical, and semi-analytic models. From dark matter to galaxy formation.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>N-body Simulations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Dark matter only (no gas)
Gravitational N-body problem
Millennium, Bolshoi, Illustris
Cosmic web structure formation
Millions to billions of particles</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Hydrodynamical Simulations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Dark matter + gas + stars
Hydrodynamics: SPH, AMR, moving mesh
Cooling, star formation, feedback
Illustris, EAGLE, FABLE
Chemical enrichment, magnetic fields</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Semi-analytic Models</h3>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Dark matter halo merger trees
Analytic prescriptions for baryonic physics
Fast: many realizations
Galform, L-Galaxies
Calibrated against observations</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Key Results</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Achievements</h3>
        <pre><code>Cosmic web reproduces observations
Galaxy luminosity function
Mass-metallicity relation
Galaxy clustering statistics
Substructure abundance</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

